{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-031", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "fc3e07cc512128cbf89af410a2b7b50a0c0df3e8509afa1186117356ace6d675", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Volumes|paragraph|Torus ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};", "msgid": "Create a torus, defined by the 3 coordinates of its center and 2 radii.\nAn additional expression defines the angular opening. @code{Torus} is\nonly available with the OpenCASCADE kernel.", "msgid_sha256": "0b20566dacba0b47d8e905076acb610f316c6312b4d169ada5c67dab72442759", "node": "Volumes", "protected_hash": "6624cf426cff584189ed7f279712356a699bfea58b05e48cc4134b135b8566f1", "protected_values": ["3", "2", "@code{Torus}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "00aaab5192aa7f3c466e6f0992f7f338e6ce3ff5401ffa0348901f208e634dd0", "semantic_key": "Torus ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "0f87ac196b7cdbeb3d4ddfa49303c4e897fcf2a0430dca398b3b55ed9ea601ca", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Volumes", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "3811b7fe45c35fb1e3aeaa894dbcdc3424c935bb8eb363c913f0d9e6cdbe5a7b"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-032", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "104f191dcde40a6b6a68cd5ec0c1182712ff8106e4e48ba8fb6bebd6e4d3a516", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Other general commands|paragraph|@var{number-option} *= @var{expression};", "msgid": "Multiply and affect @var{expression} to a real option.", "msgid_sha256": "cc98f6d48169573e707ca2f4cdc715e55103f8d50ff1596cd20f548ba186cd5b", "node": "Other general commands", "protected_hash": "2b814090be3f903569a018f7038cb2583e490c9c4b18608621a4716e18e99a00", "protected_values": ["@var{expression}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "0141fb7524d4193accf4c2c990c6a15c4c3c3a0d91e8ef827002fb8bf09a5b1a", "semantic_key": "@var{number-option} *= @var{expression};", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "fa3d69627ec788b5532a4af209f889f205b14ccaa6ae15f3bc538b08ab01abad", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Other general commands", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "6e7f1485aaef45dfaee165e3c5002856449485897c48179ab17a12655e213cde"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-033", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "ef36e30929a3bdf30c7aa3e970ca9510cab52dd0f2cf6f16d256b6a34d2193b9", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Extrusions|paragraph|7eb906c82ee923cf0dbcadfd6c0c9b8c82ff83ce9521fe2b3523aee64e2e67ea", "msgid": "Curves, surfaces and volumes can also be created through extrusion of points,\ncurves and surfaces, respectively. Here is the syntax of the geometrical\nextrusion commands (go to @ref{Structured grids}, to see how these commands\ncan be extended in order to also extrude the mesh):", "msgid_sha256": "7eb906c82ee923cf0dbcadfd6c0c9b8c82ff83ce9521fe2b3523aee64e2e67ea", "node": "Extrusions", "protected_hash": "8be8de46cf320982f9ff20f413a462b19dd01ffc172d1cb6ba23e97da6a1639f", "protected_values": ["@ref{Structured grids}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "014e4fa9b7eb44587f327fb7b3c3f711bd40b89090180aaa54b74255dafd3ea1", "semantic_key": "7eb906c82ee923cf0dbcadfd6c0c9b8c82ff83ce9521fe2b3523aee64e2e67ea", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "fe8e938e14dcece48086552b919904ad7334b8b1d65d044e3365ab3b8abd124b", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Extrusions", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "d07747d890f1cd391648c1f67248a7bc0e49ce077602a61a300f1494e165f7fe"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-034", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "81068fe56458fb7a2d99991bce860548c054a14da5548edecf7c876cc0051afb", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Built-in functions|paragraph|Atan ( @var{expression} )", "msgid": "Arc tangent (inverse tangent) of @var{expression}. Returns a value in\n[-Pi/2,Pi/2].", "msgid_sha256": "046fe9cde3438f5a2107fb2112630e2411935c6cbf583f1f0f55bb1fc63ee43c", "node": "Built-in functions", "protected_hash": "9d42621f7f06782652a621451a0b950bc0ec571b8c49db1a63f38eb897877df0", "protected_values": ["@var{expression}", "2", "2"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "016258ebf13bf708833fa5431f9d0afbc286cb7f7c55a86bb98d58d25ce7b781", "semantic_key": "Atan ( @var{expression} )", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "77b14326ba1c7a0d34689d32047aa524aabe3ab71735f5b3626362c4c7051ec9", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Built-in functions", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "501d277bb4977ae6b64c0f81c380d7cee3be31a0c4787004b5775a60e1ffd584"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-035", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "6747b33ac8265bf400d37c552104c78070fbfe6e5405ebd9b01f0f814fa8d1b3", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Structured grids|paragraph|Extrude @{ Surface @{ @var{expression-list} @}; @var{layers} < Using Index[@var{expr}]; > < Using View[@var{expr}]; > < ScaleLastLayer; > @}#2", "msgid": "The advantage of this approach is that it provides a topological\ndescription of the boundary layer, which means that it can be connected\nto other geometrical entities. The disadvantage is that the mesh is just\na ``simple'' extrusion: no fans, no special treatments of reentrant\ncorners, etc. Another boundary layer algorithm is currently available\nthrough the @code{BoundaryLayer} field (@pxref{Specifying mesh element\nsizes}). It only works in 2D however, and is a meshing constraint: it\nworks directly at the mesh level, without creating geometrical\nentities. See\ne.g. @url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/2d/BL0.geo,BL0.geo} or\n@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/2d/naca12_2d.geo,naca12_2d.geo}.", "msgid_sha256": "4773883786fef81d53da0dc8fc4d5b50c331c7675a7300e0ba2c08752f6474d0", "node": "Structured grids", "protected_hash": "c1eed34f928ebb0b161c407d9640acf5073e06a90ff04d1c3bcb0969973c87d6", "protected_values": ["@code{BoundaryLayer}", "@pxref{Specifying mesh element\nsizes}", "@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/2d/BL0.geo,", "}", "@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/2d/naca12_2d.geo,", "}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "02dec41840e37c95d2dd93cd4c81834c3cb788aba892c0b0d150bffc5c2379f5", "semantic_key": "Extrude @{ Surface @{ @var{expression-list} @}; @var{layers} < Using Index[@var{expr}]; > < Using View[@var{expr}]; > < ScaleLastLayer; > @}#2", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "fdbf0cd214bb7ad1ac05e1c1941c729cfd62cbb4dbc794ab56fd8abe098e29d6", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Structured grids", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "f527c2b0117a1d963fee846550492907150c1568f48bd3da6cb0a42c647845f4"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-036", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "da63bbf47e386cc210d4faacbe7bf00729771bd13e205de949cd3dee953dd168", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Gmsh scripting language|paragraph|1090e35849626dd4cf62f356148ebbf5d35522fa0a17022fdff5c335737102d9", "msgid": "A colon (@code{:}) after a metasyntactic variable separates the variable\nfrom its definition.", "msgid_sha256": "1090e35849626dd4cf62f356148ebbf5d35522fa0a17022fdff5c335737102d9", "node": "Gmsh scripting language", "protected_hash": "e1af5d15a1ca90288f6c4ffb6e1c95d4f11bb40a57166415fb050bc7d4650203", "protected_values": ["@code{:}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "034525ebad4f48cd3652c1f309ad58fd98350b00aa1b20929e246316e161fffa", "semantic_key": "1090e35849626dd4cf62f356148ebbf5d35522fa0a17022fdff5c335737102d9", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "b7bdd14377cc9c2c1e47a0392089339ed811641d3e73518ccf6f9986c10901b8", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Gmsh scripting language", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "1b7b213f08df526edf1032b65ea93299ec011751eb826d95e6e11eab5654d377"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-037", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "2144a20ca459f83cdf3513a6de4f9fa64592a3b0dbbe2f6d2fbde6d91ec9a23a", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Structured grids|paragraph|Extrude @{ Surface @{ @var{expression-list} @}; @var{layers} < Using Index[@var{expr}]; > < Using View[@var{expr}]; > < ScaleLastLayer; > @}", "msgid": "Extrude a ``topological'' boundary layer from the specified surfaces. If\nno view is specified, the mesh of the boundary layer entities is created\nusing a gouraud-shaded (smoothed) normal field. If a scalar view is\nspecified, it locally prescribes the thickness of the layer. If a\nvector-valued view is specified it locally prescribes both the extrusion\ndirection and the thickness. Specifying a boundary layer index allows to\nextrude several independent boundary layers (with independent normal\nsmoothing). @code{ScaleLastLayer} scales the height of the last (top)\nlayer of each normal's extrusion by the average length of the edges in\nall the source elements that contain the source node (actually, the\naverage of the averages for each element--edges actually touching the\nsource node are counted twice). This allows the height of the last layer\nto vary along with the size of the source elements in order to achieve\nbetter element quality. For example, in a boundary layer extruded with\nthe Layers definition 'Layers@{ @{1,4,2@}, @{0.5, 0.6, 1.6@} @},' a\nsource node adjacent to elements with an overall average edge length of\n5.0 will extrude to have a last layer height = (1.6-0.6) * 5.0 =\n5.0. Topological boundary layers are only available with the built-in\nkernel. See\n@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/extrude/sphere_boundary_layer.geo,sphere_boundary_layer.geo}\nor\n@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/extrude/sphere_boundary_layer_from_view.geo,sphere_boundary_layer_from_view.geo}\nfor @file{.geo} file examples, and\n@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/examples/api/aneurysm.py,aneurysm.py} for an API\nexample.", "msgid_sha256": "ddd727e4124a3ec2123ac6852158db7db84cb93c7b321b3d865c65577eeeea9e", "node": "Structured grids", "protected_hash": "6f3606dde94011d2e30ce9a7d4db10d14859532009f791d63fe1f7d759b88ffc", "protected_values": ["@code{ScaleLastLayer}", "@{", "@{", "1", "4", "2", "@}", "@{", "0.5", "0.6", "1.6", "@}", "@}", "5.0", "1.6", "0.6", "5.0", "5.0", "@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/extrude/sphere_boundary_layer.geo,", "}", "@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/benchmarks/extrude/sphere_boundary_layer_from_view.geo,", "}", "@file{.geo}", "@url{@value{GITLAB-PREFIX}/examples/api/aneurysm.py,", "}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "035076b629b2f2affbc9e3ce19e36a5cfcbcdbdf93a4ea825d60289e8476a354", "semantic_key": "Extrude @{ Surface @{ @var{expression-list} @}; @var{layers} < Using Index[@var{expr}]; > < Using View[@var{expr}]; > < ScaleLastLayer; > @}", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "1becdf42ccab7f9d4452bd8b697520786e001e4d734d459f835422931011ffbd", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Structured grids", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "2f9ed0e45f825bfeca4eae49be1fbb8020c8ab1b226ea346e96b90eae1b6d102"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-038", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "99db1000ed0af1e3a9b3d80a477bbeddc1d932409c979a2e0abb9fc05b7bfe3c", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Other general commands|paragraph|SetChanged;", "msgid": "Force the mesh and post-processing vertex arrays to be\nregenerated. Useful e.g. for creating animations with changing clipping\nplanes, etc.", "msgid_sha256": "4cbfd089dc2d3c902c65127669ed63435a40ac0eb4f4ee10205fb098d72df27b", "node": "Other general commands", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "03a8436b9ec880a1ca02edad865e939798b1d4547ff75276e8e18ff113896729", "semantic_key": "SetChanged;", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "da39ab1344d278ff23ba7b1b83ca437e15fe5e20a61f52fc5af32f45d3d260df", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Other general commands", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "8815cd574cdbb21dcb9eb2ce7b75e8a91608e4422992265e8dade0ef4056af10"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-039", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "fa223f630dac676ecb15b09a4174951c39b604dd58f6f62c16b303155b464e80", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Curves|paragraph|Compound Spline | BSpline ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} Using @var{expression};", "msgid": "Create a spline or a BSpline from control points sampled on the curves\nin @var{expression-list}. @code{Using} @var{expression} specifies the\nnumber of intervals on each curve to compute the sampling\npoints. Compound splines and BSplines are only available with the\nbuilt-in geometry kernel.", "msgid_sha256": "1e19522aa31d433c08c8a48a2632d3f7cf011998631278bf83c5b5662f2ce59a", "node": "Curves", "protected_hash": "8ab55a20769f936e38673691370b5179194b5a2b1905f75341a23e455047cb59", "protected_values": ["@var{expression-list}", "@code{Using}", "@var{expression}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "03fa5f3cb3f2571b87818479ace21ca5f3be923ec621e6ad2b7e86da373283b9", "semantic_key": "Compound Spline | BSpline ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} Using @var{expression};", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "b821a9c64089d4f854798fedb5d1b43a51e5ce769e9508467f77fa66f9fda0c5", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Curves", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "bb1b4c72abdc2b53ae065573f56c167eb51a3ff6dedd84a00384dc68a9d067d0"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-040", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "fc87327ba7db8b9520886da75e5cf17011ada6cdc9f51422a194620557c4f210", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Gmsh scripting language|paragraph|79de87c4f8937817369be6cadd612dc5269c0425dad56080bcceb8a6b404718d", "msgid": "Optional rules are enclosed in @code{<} @code{>} pairs.", "msgid_sha256": "79de87c4f8937817369be6cadd612dc5269c0425dad56080bcceb8a6b404718d", "node": "Gmsh scripting language", "protected_hash": "58e61006126742a90fbe9a672202f0748cf4f56872abbd04edbb928ed765eec0", "protected_values": ["@code{<}", "@code{>}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "07215d9732ef37fd93633e52639962ec3a99185732bec381e4fd7d3b6272197a", "semantic_key": "79de87c4f8937817369be6cadd612dc5269c0425dad56080bcceb8a6b404718d", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "d5d78d31b5abb382658ce17b8e2ab97dfe60db5968625564409876ec1b7edb3f", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Gmsh scripting language", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "e8b5b42845c6fa06f27a7fb24c74c951071d5a94554e71e82c417945247d0c58"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-041", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "18a094882b119cfa7504aa8f35bef53dfe1ac8e2721f8deb86b7161dec230c9f", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Other general commands|paragraph|Printf ( @var{string-expression} <, @var{expression-list}> );", "msgid": "Print a string expression in the information window and/or on the\nterminal. @code{Printf} is equivalent to the @code{printf} C function:\n@var{string-expression} is a format string that can contain formatting\ncharacters (@code{%f}, @code{%e}, etc.). Note that all\n@w{@var{expression}s} are evaluated as floating point values in Gmsh\n(@pxref{Floating point expressions}), so that only valid floating point\nformatting characters make sense in @var{string-expression}. See @ref{t5},\nfor an example of the use of @code{Printf}.", "msgid_sha256": "97a6914d7103f1b2c36cf76dbe4e485c0c94460c5b4991e4e0716b3f6378d119", "node": "Other general commands", "protected_hash": "e7148ef78cedd4a1fbaa9012d02e70bc5a1464f13e6158bf34744b3207759182", "protected_values": ["@code{Printf}", "@code{printf}", "@var{string-expression}", "@code{%f}", "@code{%e}", "@w{", "@var{expression}", "}", "@pxref{Floating point expressions}", "@var{string-expression}", "@ref{t5}", "@code{Printf}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "07bda0e378ab7e26498f4c1d86dcaf069c8b3855a5874709c261dc30f550730c", "semantic_key": "Printf ( @var{string-expression} <, @var{expression-list}> );", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "42f4c21be1d31cba17811983f44f62fda86f947662ba70c78d9a9d166ed27eca", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Other general commands", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "70885960adc9b9829af2da6ff2801f8be5e27392e64caba5f3cd429d38dba29d"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-042", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "0fb536ec0552ac6f63e33bf6e524af346fcbbb68b11b21416c3bfc1677796224", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Transformations|paragraph|PointsOf @{ @var{transform-list} @}", "msgid": "(Not a transformation per-se.) Return all the geometrical points on the\nboundary of the elementary entities. Useful to compute the boundary of a\ncomplex part. @value{SYNC}", "msgid_sha256": "d0d8efcf595f2c4ea9352d114fe45d0210b35f42337c0c97b51195452aee0581", "node": "Transformations", "protected_hash": "1c32f410948185d0b2385daeb8ea3eb1b3570948be8fb743f78214e26650af16", "protected_values": ["@value{SYNC}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "084a1dba6e3164799bd6d63960649ae07601ad61477ae6a2a83404b5b8305b44", "semantic_key": "PointsOf @{ @var{transform-list} @}", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi", "source_hash": "a15525640a75c545a132b833f5dbbaf2cf61a5c88f1862e6cd3814f6d5e5df91", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi::Transformations", "subcategory": "scripting", "unit_id": "088683593410baeb64f6beeca197dbfd091235ca03780547f5ed39404428c965"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-043", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "d1872f17af4cc1e09e8038b1737e11c67c7307676423a151ae10e4e83494984c", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/fltk|paragraph|gmsh/fltk/finalize", "msgid": "Close the FLTK graphical user interface. Can only be called in the main thread.", "msgid_sha256": "f4e83bd3078f6385ba7dc9adc48ec7d9807c6e5199d45e63375e3bacd55bf354", "node": "Namespace gmsh/fltk", "protected_hash": "4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945", "protected_values": [], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "0013a0152210edb23a5c3d723a844b4f75011c47db5020de3e68c40e69bd231d", "semantic_key": "gmsh/fltk/finalize", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "98304a32e106842d3c35f28588aba85862bcdfe4baf2388355408e179d370d66", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/fltk", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "bf1aec61de7057e94d750b94a12acde25b32860588e59c5b625f03db6b9b5792"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-044", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "ad1cb6ec959142096d2e43149d1004021ea7b0c122226ac09e983fb1d54a1c26", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model/mesh|paragraph|gmsh/model/mesh/setVisibility", "msgid": "Set the visibility of the elements of tags @code{elementTags} to @code{value}.", "msgid_sha256": "54c574e7a3ed642480ad3018c2d3ec58883204b44e5f1301f79047601b737ee2", "node": "Namespace gmsh/model/mesh", "protected_hash": "cd5b9d071bad01fb462e6194c115e45dc6199bf1a7166769aeb476ddf45c6815", "protected_values": ["@code{elementTags}", "@code{value}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "00ae26b8c677b8b26a31ab00c0bececa4b5a1d560a06f9607c95a341b67b4eaa", "semantic_key": "gmsh/model/mesh/setVisibility", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "20ddc7ba5b4c262f9e7867af12e2fa586417f6e653627ddd077553d1f71026cc", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/model/mesh", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "9447398804e15653d1cef59aebd9e07a85b58769ca15921574188a6ac55da364"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-045", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "8bd5ddc22b381cbb52bd6c1f6226f6690179690ab04c6c246ba1bd1269409349", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/view|paragraph|gmsh/view/setVisibilityPerWindow", "msgid": "Set the global visibility of the view @code{tag} per window to @code{value}, where @code{windowIndex} identifies the window in the window list.", "msgid_sha256": "3784904c491f54c4d411a42914c238c8715cb8c36925f391d099a82eb55bbea8", "node": "Namespace gmsh/view", "protected_hash": "b3ce2c6ad6d5c7fc9ab2f6e2ef3c41c1533eeb06e2d1aa3808ba6a7d364a9dd9", "protected_values": ["@code{tag}", "@code{value}", "@code{windowIndex}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "00c8b163860ab4eb36445a49594450899a49e3cc19b71175dd56102c52d4f93b", "semantic_key": "gmsh/view/setVisibilityPerWindow", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "84a0fd09243f79c06ee4486d20adcfc6ccbf9a018bf93efabb4b5d6072c0ac9e", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/view", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "91d0555ea550f3f98ac68759e0259b54b9dbedac994f6d208a2006f84d9ab4ac"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-046", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "0fa776b29520dcc54b1c2f7cc4f8dd5cc4a1390fe14cfaa2dd5fcef20601b69a", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/view|paragraph|gmsh/view/addListDataString", "msgid": "Add a string to a list-based post-processing view with tag @code{tag}. If @code{coord} contains 3 coordinates the string is positioned in the 3D model space (\"3D string\"); if it contains 2 coordinates it is positioned in the 2D graphics viewport (\"2D string\"). @code{data} contains one or more (for multistep views) strings. @code{style} contains key-value pairs of styling parameters, concatenated. Available keys are \"Font\" (possible values: \"Times-Roman\", \"Times-Bold\", \"Times-Italic\", \"Times-BoldItalic\", \"Helvetica\", \"Helvetica-Bold\", \"Helvetica-Oblique\", \"Helvetica-BoldOblique\", \"Courier\", \"Courier-Bold\", \"Courier-Oblique\", \"Courier-BoldOblique\", \"Symbol\", \"ZapfDingbats\", \"Screen\"), \"FontSize\" and \"Align\" (possible values: \"Left\" or \"BottomLeft\", \"Center\" or \"BottomCenter\", \"Right\" or \"BottomRight\", \"TopLeft\", \"TopCenter\", \"TopRight\", \"CenterLeft\", \"CenterCenter\", \"CenterRight\").", "msgid_sha256": "1f4b8b15393e092269c02e720d23a84e8ae6a5c603cd4d7f84a97584f0ec2260", "node": "Namespace gmsh/view", "protected_hash": "4c72c345bceabd5c912abc0dbc0715d7ca710d17496061064b2c46565f2d7337", "protected_values": ["@code{tag}", "@code{coord}", "3", "2", "@code{data}", "@code{style}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "01fe66c8e2b4ec34dc97d27cc1ffbefc6c2b6a33c2bac8b5fb360e9b4f0aa63c", "semantic_key": "gmsh/view/addListDataString", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "d15bbe8804557e60d204921ecafd0a2c7f4085a635b53a9da5ad6432cf84e164", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/view", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "3e7d365614753f96441ea857008060ca7cdf35e86d72bfd25cc3fd6f0204e04a"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-047", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "1b93d5bd28511c6a7148ecd67c5a9fd718608642b8ea4b9cc160f82c6bd32cab", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model|paragraph|gmsh/model/getColor", "msgid": "Get the color of the model entity of dimension @code{dim} and tag @code{tag}. If no color is specified for the entity, return fully transparent blue, i.e. (0, 0, 255, 0).", "msgid_sha256": "518370f5fc3a1d4619fd44c5e7e6bd5d56d12e03a02d7b2783b8642339d8119b", "node": "Namespace gmsh/model", "protected_hash": "b866e4d0c2969a1d0ccae7d183ee72f5d18f68e83f87afdbfa152978e9d792ad", "protected_values": ["@code{dim}", "@code{tag}", "0", "0", "255", "0"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "02d2d48f58df174279451b05dff400f696eb067216b90d8d42f9703d5d6d1126", "semantic_key": "gmsh/model/getColor", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "7424932ecaca25946740ec608eb7e98e3bb3e19db014b95aaeab67f4eff772e7", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/model", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "87fb6e1fa6146bdbc0a829ff15b000ff1ca0d221145ad4de5f754f96a7557262"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-048", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "f7152ece7d06c49c8456d13f4a62ac449b8a96f301a73f616eaaca7dca1b2e76", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/option|paragraph|gmsh/option/getNumber", "msgid": "Get the @code{value} of a numerical option. @code{name} is of the form \"Category.Option\" or \"Category[num].Option\". Available categories and options are listed in the @url{https://gmsh.info/doc/texinfo/gmsh.html#Gmsh-options,\"Gmsh options\" chapter of the Gmsh reference manual}.", "msgid_sha256": "596672b5027a6c5287e6eb616e01a51466a38a7065691795b46639d13954905b", "node": "Namespace gmsh/option", "protected_hash": "01d4c23d1ab605bd9ade30065faf6286397fdb582ec84a2dde23d24a3ffd2fc1", "protected_values": ["@code{value}", "@code{name}", "@url{https://gmsh.info/doc/texinfo/gmsh.html#Gmsh-options,", "}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "032628989af780900b6fc2543fd8d2f199168a457df28e7fbd38224d4c1ebd9d", "semantic_key": "gmsh/option/getNumber", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "d284de5aeab8aa713bbfcebce9a473e73e4f31cfdac398f526a5287d8e544ca5", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/option", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "447885c7b35158df9d045673149905e924e5644524711fb6993050ab4557143b"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-049", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "d3e811ecf6107ada00781bd5bb7c5cb3c063b3e850017bbcb881dbbc94b9e022", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model/occ|paragraph|gmsh/model/occ/intersect", "msgid": "Compute the boolean intersection (the common parts) of the entities @code{objectDimTags} and @code{toolDimTags} (vectors of (dim, tag) pairs) in the OpenCASCADE CAD representation. Return the resulting entities in @code{outDimTags}, and the correspondance between input and resulting entities in @code{outDimTagsMap}. If @code{tag} is positive, try to set the tag explicitly (only valid if the boolean operation results in a single entity). Remove the object if @code{removeObject} is set. Remove the tool if @code{removeTool} is set.", "msgid_sha256": "3d2df70f97bbc72379ce9b14290693c55b41a6165cb453085cc2b01640461b5d", "node": "Namespace gmsh/model/occ", "protected_hash": "5ff515024b4ddfd9046a5caa8c246b25dac2fe89b2e1b75ae0de863e65ff1954", "protected_values": ["@code{objectDimTags}", "@code{toolDimTags}", "@code{outDimTags}", "@code{outDimTagsMap}", "@code{tag}", "@code{removeObject}", "@code{removeTool}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "03a105a415f1de1b21f4f013db18e1eec795ab431b5d0443eaa62c7306b2b8cc", "semantic_key": "gmsh/model/occ/intersect", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "1eb86ad681996c0860860e615a5aefb55a9bf5bfdc9815a0ee779e11a881f61a", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/model/occ", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "119d64ebf7cbd8a81df74e58f8c5e7deb93e8fa41fe2a31c85295b8af8a749b8"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-050", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "5c40f909a20d0995d957497405f9df15c37fb4dd852ba1b4b4c4f2c7678c01de", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model/occ|paragraph|gmsh/model/occ/fillet", "msgid": "Fillet the volumes @code{volumeTags} on the curves @code{curveTags} with radii @code{radii}. The @code{radii} vector can either contain a single radius, as many radii as @code{curveTags}, or twice as many as @code{curveTags} (in which case different radii are provided for the begin and end points of the curves). Return the filleted entities in @code{outDimTags} as a vector of (dim, tag) pairs. Remove the original volume if @code{removeVolume} is set.", "msgid_sha256": "0f8fb4ca81894f1a8c5a03ea7d21ec0fd2830bbde51f38d0751f9d4739c70e4d", "node": "Namespace gmsh/model/occ", "protected_hash": "512d6f66c227aa84a1debec933710a4b9cc756c0316be6c798c6fdee30d78601", "protected_values": ["@code{volumeTags}", "@code{curveTags}", "@code{radii}", "@code{radii}", "@code{curveTags}", "@code{curveTags}", "@code{outDimTags}", "@code{removeVolume}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "03abe1b428250ec1e4e77019889468d26cd2a99badc58edbe213e2cb00f31e81", "semantic_key": "gmsh/model/occ/fillet", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "41032e3cf7f56f2088719b9b494078f9237fad5d96e9ae682a4fdc57bff0adb3", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/model/occ", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "ab4a47430fce7988029dbc81dacecc02da5eee8e260ca6b5843a56778860af51"}
{"benchmark_id": "bmk-v1-051", "category": "script_api", "context_hash": "bf366128cb99c63d2c53c9863b75568766af4a55554e30d246f721cae2f7cfdd", "msgctxt": "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model/geo|paragraph|gmsh/model/geo/addSpline", "msgid": "Add a spline (Catmull-Rom) curve in the built-in CAD representation, going through the points @code{pointTags}. If @code{tag} is positive, set the tag explicitly; otherwise a new tag is selected automatically. Create a periodic curve if the first and last points are the same. Return the tag of the spline curve.", "msgid_sha256": "08772bddbfd81f1f0e2e818fe35a0a0b57d7d47ec362f72ceb97633c4627546f", "node": "Namespace gmsh/model/geo", "protected_hash": "853dd1774fa4d35fcbad7b6653a2947df1f0004d85ec196bba2be666ba482c8e", "protected_values": ["@code{pointTags}", "@code{tag}"], "reference_translation": "", "reference_translation_status": "pending", "role": "paragraph", "schema_version": 1, "selection_method": "sha256-stratified-v1", "selection_rank": "03ac24dc1f46b824b9088a1833b2708fec55fbadeab193f292e7860001e3e956", "semantic_key": "gmsh/model/geo/addSpline", "source_file": "doc/texinfo/api.texi", "source_hash": "c04fbc46e40d4af34ce51120476afd7912b3b343e23cc81eda3aede8ee182c48", "structure_path": "doc/texinfo/api.texi::Namespace gmsh/model/geo", "subcategory": "api", "unit_id": "3d79911d20f242ee4609b581c9784b3db9366e6423865a83c85b2682f71d6260"}
